crawler (working title): credits and licences

Code: this repository (MIT, see LICENSE). Every model, texture, colour grade, effect sheet, floor and sound is
generated by code in this repository; no third-party art or audio is shipped, so there is nothing further to
attribute.

Where each asset comes from
- assets/models/hero_*, mon_*, kit_*, and the items (key, potion, elixir, food, treasure, charm, exit, teleporter,
  trap, shot_*): modelled and animated by tools/blender/crawlerchars.py and tools/blender/crawlerkit.py (with
  crawler_lib.py and cwchar_lib.py), run headless in Blender (Blender is used as a tool; its output is ours).
- assets/models/shade, ghoul, imp, slinger, ogre, hound, bloater, skitter, sporeling: hordeshooter's creatures
  (games/hordeshooter/tools/blender/hordechars.py and levelchars.py), reworked for the overhead view in crawler's
  own copies of those scripts (tools/blender/hordechars.py and levelchars.py), which build them under these names.
- assets/models/runner: hordeshooter's creature (games/hordeshooter/tools/blender/hordechars.py), as it is.
- assets/levels/*.cwmaze: tools/gen-levels.mjs. assets/lightmaps/*.cwlm and *.hash: baked by crawler_levelview
  (tools/levelview).
- assets/textures/*_floor.png, assets/grade/*.cube, assets/fx/haze.png: generated by hordeshooter's tools
  (games/hordeshooter/tools/gen-level-textures.mjs, gen-level-luts.mjs, gen-fx-sheets.mjs).
- assets/fx/fire.png, fire_mv.png, smoke.png, smoke_mv.png, scorch.png: baked by cartwheel-engine's
  tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs (procedural, CC0, listed in the engine's NOTICE).
- assets/scenes/th_*.cwscene: the tilesets' light, from hordeshooter's floor scenes.
- Sounds: synthesised in main.c.
